  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>sorafenib</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>L01EX02</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, IV dosing <small>(PK_1C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Jain L et al. 2011</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>patients with solid tumours</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>sorafenib</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_sorafenib/Sorafenib_Jain2011_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>clearance</td><td>8.13</td><td>l h(-1)</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>volume</td><td>213</td><td>l</td><td><small>V</small></td></tr><tr><td>mean absorption transit time</td><td>1.98</td><td>h</td><td><small>MTT</small></td></tr></table><h4>About sorafenib</h4><p>Sorafenib is an anticancer protein kinase inhibitor used to treat liver cancer (hepatocellular carcinoma) and kidney cancer (renal cell carcinoma), and it has also been studied for other cancers such as thyroid cancer and acute myeloid leukemia. It is authorised in the European Union and widely used in cancer care.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q421136\">Wikidata Q421136</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Sorafenib\">Sorafenib</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Jain L et al. (2011). Population pharmacokinetic analysis of sorafenib in patients with solid tumours. <i>British journal of clinical pharmacology 72(2):294–305</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-2125.2011.03963.x\">10.1111/j.1365-2125.2011.03963.x</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21392074\">21392074</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Jain_2011: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
